   "properties": {
    "Node name for S&R": "MarkdownNote"
   },
   "widgets_values": [
    "## LTX-2.5 SINGLE-STAGE keyframes + optional dialog - RTX 3090\n\n**Length**: group 2 `duration seconds` (5 -> 121 frames, 10 -> 241 frames @24fps). 10 s needs much more VRAM: use 768x448 or UD-Q5/Q4 if OOM.\n**Resolution**: width/height (/32) = final size (no upscale). Fast draft; add your own upscaler after decode if needed.\n\n**Keyframes (anti-drift)**\n- START: required. END: on by default (same characters, final positions). No END wanted -> Ctrl+B both `END guide` nodes.\n- MID-A / MID-B: bypassed. To use one: Ctrl+B its LoadImage + preprocess + **both** guide nodes.\n- Set `frame_idx` to the frame where the image must appear (e.g. 5 s: 60 = middle; 10 s: 80, 160). Use the SAME value in both stages (if 2 stages). Any position, not only the middle.\n- Keyframes must be the same scene/characters/lighting, only poses/positions change, else you get morphs/cuts.\n\n**Dialog audio (pre-generated voices)**\n- Bypassed by default -> LTX generates its own audio/speech from the prompt.\n- To use your track: Ctrl+B the 4 nodes in group 4c + `Use dialog audio` node. The audio is locked (mask 0), LTX lip-syncs the video to it. Longer audio is cut, shorter is padded and the rest is generated.\n- Make the audio the same length as the video (5 s / 10 s). Write in the prompt who says which line so the right mouth moves.\n"
   ]
  }
 ],
